# Firebase client config and store credentials. None of these have ever been
# committed - checked across all 294 commits - but nothing was stopping the
# next `git add -A` from doing it. play-service-account.json in particular is
# a real private key.
GoogleService-Info*.plist
google-services*.json
play-service-account.json
.firebaserc

# NOTE: functions/.env and functions/.env.cluttrd-staging ARE tracked, on
# purpose, and are deliberately not listed here. In Firebase Functions v2 that
# file holds defineString params, not secrets - every actual secret
# (ANTHROPIC_KEY, OPENAI_KEY, RESEND_API_KEY, the two RevenueCat webhook
# secrets, REVENUECAT_SECRET_API_KEY) uses defineSecret and lives in Secret
# Manager, never in the repo. The three values in there - CANARY_TEST_UID,
# CANARY_WEB_API_KEY, REVENUECAT_PROJECT_ID - are also written as literal
# defaults in functions/index.js, so ignoring the file would hide nothing.

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo

# generated native folders
/ios
/android
